upstream: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/greensock/gsap-skills/main/skills/gsap-plugins/SKILL.md
verified: 2026-10-02
scope: directory
reason: local retains the formerly upstream MotionPath reference and corrects its export name
note: The locally retained MotionPathHelper example now registers the documented
  `MotionPathHelper` export from `gsap/MotionPathHelper`; the old upstream text
  used the undefined identifier `MotionPathHelperPlugin` in registerPlugin().
  Upstream main still contains the MotionPath/MotionPathHelper section (line
  ~326) and still registers the undefined `MotionPathHelperPlugin` (corrected
  2026-10-08; an earlier note here wrongly said the section was removed).
would_lose_if_wired: an ordinary byte-for-byte refresh would remove the retained
  MotionPath reference, including the corrected example.
refresh_guard: _refresh-vendored.sh skips this directory when .local-fork is
  present, before any fetch or write.
to_vendor: keep the corrected local reference unless the repository decides to
  follow upstream's removal. No external publication was performed by this task.
recheck: 2026-10-02 — no upstream changes to merge; only diff is still line 331. Upstream carries the MotionPathHelper section again but
  still registers the undefined `MotionPathHelperPlugin`. npm gsap@3.15.0
  `MotionPathHelper.js` exports `MotionPathHelper` (named + default); local stays.

recheck: 2026-10-08 — further local corrections, each checked against gsap.com docs:
  Flip `nested` (prevents compounding nested movement) and `scale` (default false;
  width/height unless true) per Plugins/Flip/static.from(); Observer `type` default
  "wheel,touch,pointer" per Plugins/Observer; ScrollTo has no `element` option —
  use a selector for x/y, plus `autoKill`/`onAutoKill` per Plugins/ScrollToPlugin;
  MotionPathHelper.create(tween) or create(target, { path, ... }) per
  Plugins/MotionPathHelper (removed the undocumented helper.path/getProgress()).
  Upstream issues #19–#21 report overlapping defects; still open on 2026-10-08.
